 "heading_12": "CNC Micromachining<br/>at <span style=\"color:#F5821F\">±10 µm</span> in Polymers,<br/><span style=\"color:#F5821F\">±20 µm</span> in Metals.",
 "body_3": "<p>CNC micromachining is a high-precision subtractive manufacturing process that produces features, holes, channels, and threads at the microscopic scale, with <strong>tolerances held to ±10 µm in polymers and ±20 µm in metals</strong> and features as small as 100 µm. Goodfellow Microfabrication delivers 4-axis CNC capability combined with laser micromachining for medical, aerospace, photonics, and electronics applications.</p>",
